# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. With CRLF, macOS/Linux fails at the
# shebang with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" — an error that names a
# line ending nowhere and sends people looking at the wrong thing.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which does the
# right thing on its own; the rule is here so the guarantee does not depend on
# each contributor's local git config.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Windows batch launcher wants CRLF for the same reason, in reverse.
*.bat text eol=crlf
